#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "CAP-SECRETS Secrets and keys"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Secrets and keys live in a managed store and are fetched by identity at runtime."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Layer L1 · domain: delivery"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Hold the few secrets that remain, and the keys that protect data and state, under the platform's control."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Federation removes most secrets ([P3]{1}); what remains must never depend on one person's key. Creation-only settings cannot be fixed later, so they are decided before the first apply."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "A managed secret store per environment, reached by workload identity."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Encrypted files in repositories only with a recipient set of roles or CI."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "A values file that states each creation-only option."
msgstr ""

