#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "CAP-SECRETS.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Secrets are held in a managed secret store; none is committed in plaintext, and any encrypted file in a repository has a recipient set of roles or CI, never one person."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "A secret scanner runs on every change; encrypted files list non-personal recipients."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "CAP-SECRETS.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Settings that can only be chosen at creation, such as customer-managed keys, are decided and recorded before an environment's first apply."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "The environment's values file sets each creation-only option explicitly."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "CAP-SECRETS.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Workloads read secrets at runtime using their own identity, so no secret is copied into deployment configuration."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-secrets.md
msgid "Deployment manifests reference secrets by name, not value."
msgstr ""

